  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Washington's 5th Congressional District will determine who represents a large, Republican-leaning district spanning eastern Washington including Spokane and the surrounding counties. Incumbent Republican Michael Baumgartner, first elected in 2024, is seeking a second term in this R+5 district that covers 12 counties. A top-two primary on August 4, 2026, will narrow the field of at least nine candidates to two for the November 3 general election. The race features a rematch between Baumgartner and Democrat Carmela Conroy, who lost the 2024 general election 61%-39%, along with several other Democratic, Republican, and independent candidates competing in the nonpartisan primary.",
